@baseUrl = http://localhost:5260

# Run from top to bottom on a fresh database:
# stop the API, delete bikerental.db, start the API.
# Requests #12-#14 log in; later requests reuse their tokens.

### 1. List stations -> 200, 3 stations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stations

### 2. List bikes -> 200, paging wrapper, 5 bikes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes

### 3. Filter by type -> bikes 1 and 5
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes?type=City

### 4. Filter by status -> bikes 1-4
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes?status=Available

### 5. Filter by station -> bikes 3 and 4
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes?stationId=2

### 6. Combined filters and paging -> bike 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes?type=City&status=Available&page=1&pageSize=2

### 7. One bike -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/1

### 8. Unknown bike -> 404 BikeNotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/999

### 9. Register -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Testi",
  "lastName": "Käyttäjä",
  "email": "testi@example.com",
  "password": "Salasana123"
}

### 10. Register the same email again -> 409 EmailTaken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Testi",
  "lastName": "Käyttäjä",
  "email": "testi@example.com",
  "password": "Salasana123"
}

### 11. Wrong password -> 401 InvalidCredentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "matti@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 12. Log in as matti (Customer) -> 200
# @name loginMatti
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "matti@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 13. Log in as liisa (Customer) -> 200
# @name loginLiisa
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "liisa@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 14. Log in as admin -> 200
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 15. Own profile -> 200, Matti
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}

### 16. Profile without a token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### 17. User list as a customer -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}

### 18. User list as admin -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### 19. Create a bike without a token -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Kona Dew",
  "type": "City",
  "pricePerHour": 4.50,
  "stationId": 2
}

### 20. Create a bike as a customer -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Kona Dew",
  "type": "City",
  "pricePerHour": 4.50,
  "stationId": 2
}

### 21. Create a bike as admin -> 201, id 6
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Kona Dew",
  "type": "City",
  "pricePerHour": 4.50,
  "stationId": 2
}

### 22. Create a bike with invalid data -> 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "",
  "type": "Banana",
  "pricePerHour": 0
}

### 23. Put bike 2 into maintenance -> 200, InMaintenance
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/2
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Trek Marlin 7",
  "type": "Mountain",
  "pricePerHour": 5.00,
  "inMaintenance": true,
  "stationId": 1
}

### 24. Soft delete bike 6 -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/6
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### 25. Deleted bike -> 404 BikeNotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/6

### 26. Start a rental without a token -> 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 1
}

### 27. Matti rents bike 1 -> 201, Active, pickupStationId 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 1
}

### 28. Matti tries a second rental -> 409 UserHasActiveRental
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 4
}

### 29. Liisa tries the rented bike -> 409 BikeNotAvailable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLiisa.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 1
}

### 30. Liisa tries a bike in maintenance -> 409 BikeNotAvailable
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLiisa.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 5
}

### 31. Liisa tries an unknown bike -> 404 BikeNotFound
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLiisa.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bikeId": 999
}

### 32. Bike 1 now shows Rented
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/1

### 33. Filter rented bikes -> bike 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes?status=Rented

### 34. Rented bike into maintenance -> 409 BikeRented
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "model": "Helkama Jopo",
  "type": "City",
  "pricePerHour": 3.50,
  "inMaintenance": true,
  "stationId": 1
}

### 35. Delete the rented bike -> 409 BikeRented
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### 36. Matti's rentals -> 1 rental
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}

### 37. Liisa's rentals -> empty list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLiisa.response.body.$.token}}

### 38. Liisa opens Matti's rental -> 404 RentalNotFound (S5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLiisa.response.body.$.token}}

### 39. Liisa returns Matti's rental -> 404 RentalNotFound (S5)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/1/return
Authorization: Bearer {{loginLiisa.response.body.$.token}}

### 40. Admin sees all rentals -> includes rental 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### 41. Matti returns to station 3 -> 200, Completed, totalPrice 3.5, returnStationId 3
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/1/return
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "returnStationId": 3
}

### 42. Return again -> 409 RentalNotActive
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/1/return
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}

### 43. Bike 1 is Available at station 3
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bikes/1

### 44. Unknown rental -> 404 RentalNotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/rentals/999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}

### 45. Create a station as a customer -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/stations
Authorization: Bearer {{loginMatti.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Testi",
  "address": "Testikatu 1, 65100 Vaasa",
  "latitude": 63.09,
  "longitude": 21.61
}

### 46. Create a station as admin -> 201, id 4
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/stations
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Keskussairaala",
  "address": "Hietalahdenkatu 2-4, 65130 Vaasa",
  "latitude": 63.0868,
  "longitude": 21.5833
}

### 47. Update the station -> 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/stations/4
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Vaasan keskussairaala",
  "address": "Hietalahdenkatu 2-4, 65130 Vaasa",
  "latitude": 63.0868,
  "longitude": 21.5833
}

### 48. Delete a station with bikes -> 409 StationHasBikes (S10)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/stations/3
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### 49. Delete an empty station -> 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/stations/4
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.token}}

### 50. Deleted station -> 404 StationNotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/stations/4